From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:22:06 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): skill_manage create asks to extend an
 overlapping skill

With skills.create_overlap_threshold above 0 (default 0 = off, upstream's behavior), a create whose name or description overlaps an installed skill is refused with the top 3 matches (token overlap on name and description, no model call). The agent patches one of them, or repeats the create with why_new, one sentence on why none fits, and it proceeds. The tool description now says: extend an existing skill when one covers the topic; create only for a new topic. A lookup error lets the create through.
